#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0282 expect=skipped domain=PP
#note "Requirements.Variables.All is the literal [PPSPEC] and the column is not declared, so ScopeMatcher rejects the dataset and the rule is NOT EXECUTED. Untouched by M3-D7. Note the rule does not ship in rules-cdisc-sendig-3-0.json (its sheet rows start at SENDIG v3.1, Release Notes 'Replaces SEND Rule 197'), so version=3-1-1 is load-bearing on all four of its scenarios."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#library codelist-terms SPEC SERUM URINE PLASMA "WHOLE BLOOD"
dataset PP class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetics Parameters"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PPSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PPTESTCD type=Char label="Parameter Short Name"
---
S1 | PP | 001 | 1 | CLR
S1 | PP | 002 | 2 | AUCALL
---
